{% extends 'layout.twig' %}

{% macro status(kind) %}
  {%- if kind == 'shipped' -%}<span class="rm-status rm-status-shipped"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Shipped</span>
  {%- elseif kind == 'progress' -%}<span class="rm-status rm-status-progress"><span aria-hidden="true">◐</span> In progress</span>
  {%- elseif kind == 'later' -%}<span class="rm-status rm-status-later"><span aria-hidden="true">○</span> Later</span>
  {%- else -%}<span class="rm-status rm-status-planned"><span aria-hidden="true">○</span> Planned</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{% block body %}
{% import _self as rm %}
  <div class="card roadmap-page">
    <h2>Roadmap</h2>
    <p class="lede">Here are the things on our to do list. If there is something that bugs you about OSM or something which is missing, let us know and we can see if it is possible.</p>
    <p class="muted">This page is also the changelog: what went live and when is listed under <a href="#history">Changelog</a>, newest first.</p>

    <div class="rm-legend" aria-label="Status key">
      <span class="rm-legend-title">Key:</span>
      <span class="rm-key">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <span class="rm-legend-text">live now, with the date it went live</span></span>
      <span class="rm-key">{{ rm.status('progress') }} <span class="rm-legend-text">being built</span></span>
      <span class="rm-key">{{ rm.status('planned') }} <span class="rm-legend-text">next up</span></span>
      <span class="rm-key">{{ rm.status('later') }} <span class="rm-legend-text">backlog</span></span>
    </div>

    <p class="rm-jump muted">Jump to: <a href="#shipped">Shipped</a> · <a href="#history">Changelog</a> · <a href="#in-progress">In progress</a> · <a href="#planned">Planned</a> · <a href="#later">Later</a></p>

    <section class="help-section" id="shipped" aria-labelledby="shipped-h">
      <h3 id="shipped-h">Shipped</h3>
      <p class="muted">Newest first. The <a href="#history">Changelog</a> below has the details.</p>
      <ul class="rm-list">
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Waiting list</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">WordPress joining form</h4>
          <p>A waiting-list form for your group’s WordPress website. Parents fill it in and OSMHelper adds the child to your OSM waiting list with your OSM login, so there’s no OSM app to set up for each group. Includes a parent note, confirmation email, address lookup, text-message consent and optional captcha. Set it up under Members → Joining form.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-26">26 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Waiting list</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Waiting list rank, dated notes and willing to help</h4>
          <p>Rank applicants, add dated notes and mark who is willing to help, then review and save to your own OSM custom fields. Works with more than one waiting list. The score is explained on the page and stays in OSMHelper.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-26">26 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Site</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Changelog</h4>
          <p>A dated list of what’s new. Since 28 Sep 2026 it’s part of this page, under <a href="#history">Changelog</a>.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-21">21 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Badges</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Nights Away tracker</h4>
          <p>Pick one or more members with search (Leaders and Young Leaders are left out) to see nights away per camp from OSM, including named Discovery camps. Sort across members, filter by year, and export to PDF with the scout’s name and totals.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Badges</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Top awards</h4>
          <p>Pick a section to see how close each member is to their top award (Chief Scout’s award), review the suggested progress, then confirm to write it to OSM. Updated on 7 and 8 Sep 2026 with Bronze and Silver awards and rate-limit warnings.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Finance</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Bank accounts, transactions and All transfers</h4>
          <p>Read your OSM bank accounts and transactions, and see transfers across all accounts with unmatched in/out legs flagged.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Equipment</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Equipment list, bulk move and locations</h4>
          <p>All your OSM equipment columns in one searchable table, broken items highlighted, and bulk moves to locations you set up in Settings.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Members</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Members, member checks and group numbers</h4>
          <p>Members across sections, checks for missing details, the waiting list, and group numbers with bar charts by section.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Site</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Menus, tables, Help and Roadmap</h4>
          <p>Grouped menus with icons, tables you can sort, search and export, the OSM rate limit shown on screen, and the Help and Roadmap pages.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="history" aria-labelledby="history-h">
      <h3 id="history-h">Changelog</h3>
      <p class="muted">What changed, newest first. Each entry went live on the date shown.</p>
      <ul class="rm-list">
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-05">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">WordPress joining form</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Waiting-list form for your website:</strong> a WordPress plugin adds a form with the <code>[osm_waiting_list]</code> shortcode. When a parent sends it, OSMHelper adds the child to your OSM waiting list using your OSM login. Parents don’t need an OSM login, and groups don’t need their own OSM app or API keys.</li>
            <li><strong>What’s saved in OSM:</strong> the child’s name, date of birth and home address (line 1, line 2, town, county, postcode), and up to two parents as Primary Contacts 1 and 2.</li>
            <li><strong>Text messages:</strong> each parent can tick “Receive text messages from Leaders?”, which turns on OSM’s receive-texts setting for their phone.</li>
            <li><strong>Parent note:</strong> an optional note is added to the waiting list’s Notes field (the one chosen in Rank &amp; notes) as a dated line marked “Parent (website form)”. If no Notes field is chosen, the child is still added.</li>
            <li><strong>In WordPress:</strong> a confirmation email to parents with your own reply-to address, Google reCAPTCHA or Cloudflare Turnstile against spam, and address lookup with Google address search or a free postcodes.io postcode check.</li>
            <li><strong>Joining form page:</strong> a new <a href="/wordpress-form/">Members → Joining form</a> page has the plugin download, your site key and waiting-list choice (moved from Settings), step-by-step setup and troubleshooting.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-09-28">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-28">28 Sep 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Clearer homepage, one Roadmap and changelog page</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>New homepage:</strong> a plainer, first-person homepage with real screenshots of the tools (all using made-up names), a short note on why OSMHelper exists, and a clear “Before you connect” section.</li>
            <li><strong>One page for plans and changes:</strong> the Changelog is now part of this Roadmap page. Old <code>/changelog/</code> links bring you here.</li>
            <li><strong>Menu on phones:</strong> when you’re not signed in, the Menu button now shows on small screens, so Home, Help and Roadmap can be reached.</li>
            <li><strong>Footer and contact:</strong> the footer now says who runs OSMHelper and that it isn’t made or endorsed by Online Scout Manager or The Scout Association. The contact address is now hello@jonbloor.co.uk.</li>
            <li><strong>Less kept on the server:</strong> Top awards results are deleted from the server after 2 hours and when you log out, debug files are off, and the error log strips names and contact details.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-09-27">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-27">27 Sep 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Clearer roadmap</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Status at a glance:</strong> the <a href="/roadmap/">Roadmap</a> now groups items as Shipped, In progress, Planned and Later. Each item has a labelled badge with a symbol, not just a colour, and there’s a key at the top.</li>
            <li><strong>Dates:</strong> shipped items show the date they went live, newest first. The Nights Away tracker, Top awards, Finance, Equipment and Members tools are now listed as shipped.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-09-26">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-26">26 Sep 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Waiting list ranking</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Rank &amp; notes:</strong> leaders can give each applicant a rank (1 = first to be offered a place) and add notes, then review exactly what will change before saving to OSM. Values live in your own OSM custom fields; OSMHelper only remembers which fields to use, shared across your group.</li>
            <li><strong>Dated notes:</strong> a new note is added at the top of the existing notes as <code>dd/mm/yy hh:mm - your name - "note"</code> (UK time), so earlier notes are kept.</li>
            <li><strong>Willing to help:</strong> optionally choose an OSM field for it on the Fields page. It can be set to Yes, No or blank from the ranking page and adds 20 to the score when it’s yes.</li>
            <li><strong>More than one waiting list:</strong> pick a list at the top of each page; each list is set up separately.</li>
            <li><strong>Score explained:</strong> the Waiting list and ranking pages now say how the score works, and hovering over or tapping a score shows the breakdown. The score stays in OSMHelper and is never saved to OSM.</li>
            <li><strong>Safer saving:</strong> changes are re-read from OSM before saving, saved one at a time (stopping at the first problem), then checked in OSM; the results page shows what was sent and what OSM now holds.</li>
            <li><strong>Exports:</strong> CSV, Excel and PDF from the Waiting list and ranking pages include every row (even when searching) and the values you’ve typed.</li>
            <li><strong>Menus:</strong> the Members, Badges and Finance menus now close when you click elsewhere, press Escape or choose an item.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="in-progress" aria-labelledby="in-progress-h">
      <h3 id="in-progress-h">In progress</h3>
      <p class="muted">Nothing is being built right now. The next job will come from the Planned list below.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="planned" aria-labelledby="planned-h">
      <h3 id="planned-h">Planned</h3>
      <ul class="rm-list">
        <li class="rm-item rm-planned">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('planned') }} <span class="rm-area">Equipment</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Add and edit equipment items</h4>
          <p>Create and update quartermaster items in OSM from OSMHelper.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-planned">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('planned') }} <span class="rm-area">Badges</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Badge spreadsheet upload</h4>
          <p>Upload a CSV or Excel file, match its columns, check a dry run, then save the badges to OSM.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="later" aria-labelledby="later-h">
      <h3 id="later-h">Later</h3>
      <ul class="rm-list">
        <li class="rm-item rm-later">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('later') }} <span class="rm-area">Programme</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Complete Programme printout</h4>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-later">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('later') }} <span class="rm-area">Programme</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Term Summary printout</h4>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-later">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('later') }} <span class="rm-area">Badges</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Challenge badge printout</h4>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-later">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('later') }} <span class="rm-area">Members</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Tidier duplicate checks</h4>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-later">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('later') }} <span class="rm-area">Sections</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Section overview</h4>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="requests">
      <h3>Feature requests</h3>
      <p>Got an idea? Email <a href="mailto:hello@jonbloor.co.uk">hello@jonbloor.co.uk</a>.</p>
      <p class="muted"><a href="/help/">Help</a> explains what works today, and the <a href="#history">Changelog</a> above lists what’s new.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script>
    // /changelog/ 301s to /roadmap/?from=changelog (no fragment). Browsers keep the original fragment on a
    // fragment-less redirect, so old links like /changelog/#2026-09-26 still land on that entry. With no
    // fragment, jump to the Changelog section. Either way, drop ?from= from the address bar.
    (function () {
      var q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      if (q.get('from') !== 'changelog') return;
      var hash = location.hash;
      if (!hash) {
        var h = document.getElementById('history');
        if (h) h.scrollIntoView();
        hash = '#history';
      }
      if (history.replaceState) history.replaceState(null, '', location.pathname + hash);
    })();
  </script>
{% endblock %}
